<h1>Privacy policy</h1>
<p class="error" role="status">Draft pending publisher approval. Hosting log, backup and cleanup retention must be confirmed before this policy is published.</p>
<p>AgentRAG is operated by Mathieu MOUBRI. Contact: <a href="mailto:mathieu.moubri@gmail.com">mathieu.moubri@gmail.com</a>.</p>
<h2>Information processed</h2>
<p>Account email and identifiers; Google sign-in profile/identifier when selected; document titles and text, chunks and embeddings; questions and relevant conversation context; OAuth authorizations/tokens; and technical request/error information needed to operate the service.</p>
<h2>Purpose and recipients</h2>
<p>Data are used to authenticate you, maintain your knowledge base, retrieve passages, generate answers and citations, and investigate failures. The site and PostgreSQL database are hosted by MonsterASP.NET in Europe. Azure AI Foundry in Sweden processes model and embedding inputs, including questions and relevant document content. Google processes Google sign-in. The client you connect, including ChatGPT or Codex, receives requested tool results and processes its own conversation history under its own policies.</p>
<h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
<p>Account data remain while your account exists. Documents, chunks and embeddings remain until you delete a document or your account is deleted. Document deletion removes its chunks from the active database. Chat conversations are not persisted in the AgentRAG database. OAuth access tokens last one hour; refresh tokens last 30 days with rotation and revocation. Expired OAuth records may remain until cleanup.</p>
<p>Provider backups, disaster-recovery copies and infrastructure logs have their own retention. Their exact durations for this deployment are being verified; no immediate deletion of every provider copy is asserted.</p>
<h2>Your choices</h2>
<p>Delete documents in the website, disconnect clients, revoke Google access in your Google account, or contact the publisher for account deletion, access or correction requests. Identity verification may be required. Applicable legal rights are preserved.</p>
